import scene_poses.dl
import scene_mesh.dl
import scene_angles.dl

class:
    patterns:
        UI scene orbit coordinates
    members:
        yaw as a floating-point number
        polar as a floating-point number
        distance as a floating-point number

class:
    patterns:
        UI scene orbit
    members:
        camera as UI scene camera
        up as UI scene vector
        north as UI scene vector
        east as UI scene vector
        yaw as a floating-point number
        polar as a floating-point number
        distance as a floating-point number
        desired yaw as a floating-point number
        desired polar as a floating-point number
        desired distance as a floating-point number
        desired target as UI scene vector
        minimum distance as a floating-point number
        maximum distance as a floating-point number
        minimum polar as a floating-point number
        maximum polar as a floating-point number
        retention as a floating-point number
        start yaw as a floating-point number
        start polar as a floating-point number
        start distance as a floating-point number
        start target as UI scene vector
        elapsed as a floating-point number
        duration as a floating-point number

to get [the coordinates of UI scene camera] {UI scene camera:camera} [in orbit] {a pointer to UI scene orbit:orbit}:
    set checked to the UI scene view matrix for camera
    set relative to camera's position - camera's target
    set east to the dot product of relative and (orbit's east)
    set north to the dot product of relative and (orbit's north)
    set up to the dot product of relative and (orbit's up)
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI scene orbit coordinates, @intrinsic("atan2", east, north), @intrinsic("atan2", the square root of (east * east + north * north), up), the length of relative)

to [place UI scene orbit] {a pointer to UI scene orbit:orbit}:
    set horizontal to (orbit's north) * (the cosine of orbit's yaw) + (orbit's east) * (the sine of orbit's yaw)
    set direction to horizontal * (the sine of orbit's polar) + (orbit's up) * (the cosine of orbit's polar)
    set orbit's camera's position to orbit's camera's target + direction * orbit's distance

to [settle UI scene orbit] {a pointer to UI scene orbit:orbit}:
    set orbit's yaw to orbit's desired yaw
    set orbit's polar to orbit's desired polar
    set orbit's distance to orbit's desired distance
    set orbit's camera's target to orbit's desired target
    set orbit's duration to 0.0
    place UI scene orbit orbit

to [cancel UI scene orbit focus] {a pointer to UI scene orbit:orbit}:
    if orbit's duration = 0.0:
        return nothing
    set orbit's duration to 0.0
    set orbit's desired yaw to orbit's yaw
    set orbit's desired polar to orbit's polar
    set orbit's desired distance to orbit's distance
    set orbit's desired target to orbit's camera's target

to get [a UI scene orbit for] {UI scene camera:camera} [between distances] {floating-point number:near} [and] {floating-point number:far} [and polar angles] {floating-point number:low} [and] {floating-point number:high}:
    require condition (((near is finite) and (far is finite)) and (0.0 < near <= far)) reporting "Scene orbit distance limits must be finite and positive"
    require condition ((0.0 < low <= high) and (high < 3.141592653589793)) reporting "Scene orbit polar limits must stay strictly between its poles"
    set result to a new UI scene orbit
    set result's camera to camera
    set result's up to camera's up normalized
    set reference to a UI scene vector from [0.0,0.0,1.0]
    if (the absolute value of result's up's z) > 0.9:
        set reference to a UI scene vector from [0.0,1.0,0.0]
    set result's north to (reference - (result's up) * (the dot product of reference and (result's up))) normalized
    set result's east to the cross product of (result's up) and (result's north)
    set result's minimum distance to near
    set result's maximum distance to far
    set result's minimum polar to low
    set result's maximum polar to high
    set result's retention to 0.85
    set coordinates to the coordinates of UI scene camera camera in orbit (the address of result)
    set result's desired yaw to coordinates's yaw
    set result's desired polar to coordinates's polar clamped between low and high
    set result's desired distance to coordinates's distance clamped between near and far
    set result's desired target to camera's target
    settle UI scene orbit (the address of result)
    return result
